-- title:
--   Left D^×-equivariance of the idelic lattice dictionary
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$, let $\delta$ be a unit of $D$, and let $g$ be a unit of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ relative to $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. Recall the two constructions involved. First, [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda$ is the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ generated by the elements $z \otimes a$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $a$ a finite adele lying in $\mathcal{O}_v$ at every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. Second, [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda\, g$ is the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ consisting of those $z \in D$ whose image $z \otimes 1$ under $D \to D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ lies in the left translate of that box by $g$, i.e. the preimage of $g \cdot (\text{box})$ along the inclusion of the left factor. Finally, [`Submodule.finiteIdeleDiagonal`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L43) sends $\delta \in D^{\times}$ to the unit $\delta \otimes 1$. The assertion is the equality of $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $D$ $$\text{ofFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda\,\bigl((\delta \otimes 1)\, g\bigr) = \delta \cdot \text{ofFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda\, g,$$ the right-hand side being the pointwise action of the unit $\delta$ on the submodule, i.e. the set of products $\delta y$ with $y$ in $\text{ofFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda\, g$. No hypothesis is imposed on $\Lambda$.
--
--   This is the left $D^{\times}$-equivariance of the dictionary $g \mapsto D \cap g\widehat{\Lambda}$ between finite ideles of $D$ and $\mathbb{Z}$-lattices in $D$: the dictionary intertwines left multiplication by global units with homothety of lattices, so that, combined with right invariance under the stabiliser of the box, it descends to a map from a double coset space to lattices up to left $D^{\times}$-homothety. It is used throughout the class-set and coset-graph computations for Eichler orders in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, for instance in identifying quotients of vertices and edges with class sets and in the criterion for equality of classes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_ofFiniteIdele_diagonal_mul.lean

